From e97ed44c4f201f5bc05fabcb2467b973938ad077 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:49:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 101/112] Volume knobs: 0.5 dB per detent, shown in dB (menus
 and gold knobs)

A sound's and a kit row's level, a kit's, an audio track's and the song's volume, in their menus and on the gold
knob (LEVEL), step by 0.5 dB per detent and show dB (OLED "-3.5 dB", "+12.0 dB", "-inf dB"; 7-segment "-3.5",
"12.0", "OFF"). Below -60 dB comes off. The stored value and the x^2 gain law stay (modulation/params/
volume_steps.h), so saved songs keep their exact level and files load both ways; automation, MIDI and cables keep
the stored domain. A value between the steps (old songs, automation) shows to 0.1 dB, and the first detent takes it
to the 0.5 dB grid in the direction turned. Sound/kit row: 0 dB at the old 25, up to +12.0; kit/audio track/song:
0 dB at the old 35.4 (their >> 1), up to +6.0 (the kit's x1.25 and the audio track's x1.2196 headroom factors are
not counted).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
